1
00:00:18,460 --> 00:00:20,620
我們要穿越意大利的葡萄園
We're taking a four-week bicycle trip

2
00:00:20,620 --> 00:00:21,720
完成一次為期四周的自行車旅行
through the vineyards of Italy!

3
00:00:22,099 --> 00:00:24,119
我們認為今年夏天 海莉 迪蘭
We figure that this summer, our whole lives

4
00:00:24,119 --> 00:00:25,509
還有他們的雙胞胎寶寶搬進來以后
are gonna be turned upside-down

5
00:00:25,509 --> 00:00:28,879
我們的生活會被攪得天翻地覆
when Haley, Dylan, and their twins move in with us,

6
00:00:28,879 --> 00:00:32,049
所以干嘛不度個"外孫月"放松一下呢
so why not splurge on a grandbaby-moon?

7
00:00:32,080 --> 00:00:33,600
因此我們一直在聽語言學習帶
So we've been hitting the language tapes,

8
00:00:33,679 --> 00:00:35,669
騎固定腳踏車
the, uh -- the stationary bikes,

9
00:00:35,669 --> 00:00:38,299
而且我還一天對克萊爾吹好幾次流氓哨
and a couple of times a day, I wolfishly whistle at Claire

10
00:00:38,299 --> 00:00:40,909
讓她為羅馬人的經典熱情做好準備
to prepare her for that timeless Roman charm.

11
00:00:41,660 --> 00:00:44,600
我不敢相信我們在弗里特利餐館
I can't believe after all those nights at Fratelli's

12
00:00:44,600 --> 00:00:45,540
聊了那么多次要去意大利之后
talking about going to Italy,

13
00:00:45,540 --> 00:00:46,960
我們真的要去了
it's actually happening.

14
00:00:47,209 --> 00:00:49,389
美國夫人
Ohh, American lady!

15
00:00:49,389 --> 00:00:51,398
為什么你要這么對我
Why do you do this to me?

16
00:00:51,398 --> 00:00:53,748
別再逼我對你練習扇耳光了
Don't make me practice my slap on you again. Mm.

17
00:00:53,840 --> 00:00:54,620
怎么了
What's that?

18
00:00:54,620 --> 00:00:56,740
我在等電話 我為咱們的周年紀念
Oh, I'm on hold. I'm booking us

19
00:00:56,740 --> 00:00:58,920
給咱倆預定了托斯卡納的一座
into a converted castle in Tuscany

20
00:00:58,920 --> 00:01:00,580
-翻新城堡 -它有護城河嗎
- for our anniversary. - Does it have a moat?

21
00:01:00,800 --> 00:01:03,440
我一直在處理我們所有的稅單
I've been working on all of our receipts for taxes.

22
00:01:03,520 --> 00:01:04,520
我們很可能得到一筆退款
Looks like we're getting a refund,

23
00:01:04,680 --> 00:01:06,700
那就意味著我們能夠負擔得起...
which means that we can afford to --

24
00:01:06,738 --> 00:01:08,198
讓小矮人放下護城河上的吊橋
To pay the dwarf who will lower the drawbridge

25
00:01:08,198 --> 00:01:09,819
只要我們能夠回答出他的三個謎語
if we answer his riddles three?

26
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:11,860
讓我先斷了你的念想 沒有護城河
I'm gonna nip this in the bud. No moat.

27
00:01:12,268 --> 00:01:14,048
這趟旅行真是個好主意
This trip was such a great idea.

28
00:01:14,048 --> 00:01:16,028
我知道
Oh, I know.

29
00:01:16,128 --> 00:01:18,358
今年夏天這兒會一直忙忙碌碌的
Things are gonna be so hectic here this summer.

30
00:01:18,358 --> 00:01:19,628
好詭異 一想到有人稱呼我們為外公
It's weird to think people will be calling us

31
00:01:19,628 --> 00:01:21,378
-和... -別說 千萬別說
- Grandpa and -- - No, please don't say it.

32
00:01:21,378 --> 00:01:23,698
別說那個詞 它讓我覺得自己好老
Don't say that word. It makes me feel so old.

33
00:01:23,760 --> 00:01:25,500
但我想過讓他們叫我什么了
But I have thought about what I want them to call me.

34
00:01:26,900 --> 00:01:27,920
-阿嬤 -阿嬤
- Gammy. - Gammy.

35
00:01:28,620 --> 00:01:29,740
行 我們試試這詞怎么樣
Well, let's take her for a spin.

36
00:01:30,180 --> 00:01:31,500
"大家注意 阿嬤來啦"
"Hey, everyone, Gammy's here!"

37
00:01:32,040 --> 00:01:34,400
"抱歉 今天不行 阿嬤心情不好"
"Sorry, guys, not today, Gammy's in a mood."

38
00:01:34,468 --> 00:01:36,777
不錯啊 這詞行
Yeah, it does. It works. Mm. Yeah.

39
00:01:36,780 --> 00:01:38,620
-嗨 室友們 -嗨..."室友"
- Hey, roomies. - Hey -- "Roomies"?

40
00:01:38,880 --> 00:01:40,880
拿這些箱子和袋子做什么
What is with all the boxes and the bags?

41
00:01:41,060 --> 00:01:43,640
我知道我們說會等寶寶出生再搬進來
Well, I know we said we'd move in when the babies come,

42
00:01:43,640 --> 00:01:45,720
但是后來我們想到早搬來早省錢
but then we thought about all the money we'd save.

43
00:01:46,000 --> 00:01:46,700
許許多多錢[西語]
Mucho dinero.

44
00:01:47,920 --> 00:01:49,040
-好 -你看起來很生氣
- Yes. - You look mad.

45
00:01:49,137 --> 00:01:51,047
我應該先告訴你的 我很害怕跟你說
I should've told you. I was afraid to tell you.

46
00:01:51,047 --> 00:01:52,667
因為如果你不樂意 我怕自己應付不來
I didn't think that I could handle the disappointment

47
00:01:52,667 --> 00:01:54,357
隨之而來的失望
if you weren't happy about it.

48
00:01:54,357 --> 00:01:55,877
但你沒有不開心吧 對嗎
But you're not unhappy about it, right?

49
00:01:55,980 --> 00:01:57,620
-是吧 -親愛的 親愛的
- Right?! - Oh, honey. Oh, honey.

50
00:01:57,657 --> 00:02:00,767
我的天 你最好了 我太愛你了
Oh, my gosh, you're the best. I love you so much.

51
00:02:01,800 --> 00:02:03,720
好一趟高潮迭起的情緒之旅啊
Wow! What a journey.

52
00:02:04,100 --> 00:02:06,580
等我荷爾蒙開始作亂了 生活會是什么樣啊
What is my life gonna be like when I'm in the hormonal stage?

53
00:02:06,657 --> 00:02:07,807
等一下 還有一件事情
Oh, wait, there was one more thing, um...

54
00:02:07,807 --> 00:02:09,747
我該把這些箱子放在哪兒
Hey, where should I put these boxes?

55
00:02:09,747 --> 00:02:11,367
我媽突然來了
My mom surprised us. We were hoping

56
00:02:11,380 --> 00:02:12,480
我們希望她能暫住幾天
she could stay a couple days.

57
00:02:13,140 --> 00:02:14,420
你們好 你們好
Hello, hello!

58
00:02:15,407 --> 00:02:17,987
我們也是時候該正式見面了
Well, it's about time we officially met,

59
00:02:17,987 --> 00:02:20,747
考慮到我們的基因已經在海莉的子宮里
considering our DNA is already swirling around

60
00:02:20,760 --> 00:02:22,080
難舍難分了
in Haley's womb.

61
00:02:23,636 --> 00:02:24,587
菲爾
Phil.

62
00:02:24,780 --> 00:02:25,340
你好
Oh, hey.

63
00:02:26,060 --> 00:02:27,280
-克萊爾 -你好
- Claire. - Oh, hi.

64
00:02:28,560 --> 00:02:29,780
-我是法拉 -你好 法拉
- I'm Farrah. - Hi, Farrah.

65
00:02:30,200 --> 00:02:32,560
-你看起來好眼熟 -我在抗議活動中
- You look so familiar. - Well, I meet a lot of people

66
00:02:32,560 --> 00:02:34,300
認識了很多人
with my work in the protest movement.

67
00:02:34,820 --> 00:02:37,440
你參加過"象牙就是謀殺"樂跑活動嗎
Oh, did you participate in the Ivory is Murder Fun Run?

68
00:02:37,580 --> 00:02:40,160
-沒印象 -親愛的 不如你帶法拉
- Not that I recall. - Sweetheart, why don't you show Farrah

69
00:02:40,160 --> 00:02:42,000
-看看她要睡在哪里吧 -不用了
- where she will be sleeping. - Oh, no,

70
00:02:42,016 --> 00:02:43,846
我只需要兩個承重鉤子
I just need two weight-bearing hooks

71
00:02:43,846 --> 00:02:45,476
間隔七英尺就行了
spaced seven feet apart.

72
00:02:45,476 --> 00:02:47,596
這件和服可以變成吊床
This kimono converts to a hammock.

73
00:02:48,356 --> 00:02:50,206
-準備就緒[意語] -意大利
- Pronto! - Italy!

74
00:02:50,206 --> 00:02:51,596
-他們回復了 我手機呢 -糟糕糟糕
- They answered! Where's the phone? - Oh! Oh, no, no, no.

75
00:02:51,596 --> 00:02:53,016
-手機去哪兒了 -找到了 這兒呢
- Where's the phone? - I got it, right here.

76
00:02:53,016 --> 00:02:54,377
找到了嗎 我接住了
You got it? Get it.

77
00:02:55,236 --> 00:02:56,446
兄弟 我很抱歉
Oh! Oh, buddy, I'm so sorry.

78
00:02:56,446 --> 00:02:57,826
-我給你拿點冰塊 -該死
- Let me get you some ice. - Damn it!

79
00:02:57,826 --> 00:03:00,206
別擔心 我帶了磁石
No, no, don't worry. I brought magnets.

80
00:03:01,080 --> 00:03:02,860
她就這么處理頭部受傷嗎
Is that the way she treats all head injuries?

81
00:03:02,920 --> 00:03:04,020
這讓我有了個理論
Because I've got a theory.

82
00:03:19,145 --> 00:03:21,925
我想把這些舊玩具送給海莉的寶寶們
I want to give these old toys to Haley's babies.

83
00:03:22,200 --> 00:03:24,320
喬 你太有心了
Oh, Joe, that's so sweet!

84
00:03:24,620 --> 00:03:27,460
現在我的壁柜里有地方放蜥蜴了
Now I have room in the closet for my lizard.

85
00:03:28,060 --> 00:03:29,820
蜥蜴 我以為你們只是去寵物店
Lizard? I thought that you were just

86
00:03:29,820 --> 00:03:31,460
看一下而已
going to the pet shop to look.

87
00:03:31,480 --> 00:03:33,220
我沒法對那張小臉說不
I can't say no to that face.

88
00:03:33,365 --> 00:03:35,605
你得在他青春期前一直唱紅臉了
You're gonna have to be bad cop 'til puberty,

89
00:03:35,605 --> 00:03:36,935
等到普里契特的喉結
you know, when the Pritchett Adam's apple

90
00:03:36,935 --> 00:03:38,715
和小胡茬冒出來的時候
and fuzz-stache show up.

91
00:03:38,715 --> 00:03:42,155
曼尼 你也應該給雙胞胎點東西
Manny, you should also give something for the twins.

92
00:03:42,155 --> 00:03:44,065
你們都要當舅舅了
You both are gonna be uncles.

93
00:03:44,065 --> 00:03:46,965
這在我們家是項光榮的傳統
That's a very proud tradition in our family.

94
00:03:46,965 --> 00:03:49,775
說得沒錯 喬 我們的先祖阿爾瓦羅
That's right, Joe. Our great-great Uncle Alvaro

95
00:03:49,775 --> 00:03:51,945
是位有名的南美解放斗士
was a famous South American freedom fighter.

96
00:03:51,945 --> 00:03:53,774
你開玩笑嗎 我的先祖伊拉茲馬斯
You're kidding? My Great Uncle Erasmus

97
00:03:53,774 --> 00:03:55,184
是阿拉莫戰爭中的英雄
was a hero at the Alamo.

98
00:03:55,220 --> 00:03:57,120
我們再多說幾句就會發現
We're four sentences away from realizing

99
00:03:57,120 --> 00:03:58,460
他們互相殘殺了吧
they killed each other, right?

100
00:03:59,040 --> 00:04:00,700
喬 下周你要打扮成英雄
Joe, next week, you have to go

101
00:04:00,700 --> 00:04:01,900
去學校
to school dressed as a hero.

102
00:04:02,040 --> 00:04:04,140
為什么不打扮成先祖阿爾瓦羅呢
Why don't you dress as Uncle Alvaro?

103
00:04:04,260 --> 00:04:05,520
還是先祖伊拉茲馬斯好
Or Uncle Erasmus.

104
00:04:05,964 --> 00:04:07,684
杰 好傻好天真
Ay, Jay, that's cute,

105
00:04:07,740 --> 00:04:10,380
阿爾瓦羅可不只是個戰爭英雄
but Alvaro was not only a war hero.

106
00:04:10,380 --> 00:04:12,980
他還是有名的斗牛士
He was a celebrated matador,

107
00:04:13,360 --> 00:04:15,660
弗里達·卡羅[天才女畫家]的探戈導師
Frida Kahlo's tango instructor,

108
00:04:15,660 --> 00:04:18,340
波哥大先驅報小漫畫比賽的
two-time winner of the Bogota Herald

109
00:04:18,340 --> 00:04:20,960
兩屆冠軍
cartoon caption contest.

110
00:04:21,174 --> 00:04:23,284
沒有冒犯的意思 不過我覺得他連給
No disrespect, but I don't think he was fit to shine

111
00:04:23,284 --> 00:04:25,444
伊拉茲馬斯·杰·普里契特擦鞋都不配
Erasmus J. Pritchett's boots,

112
00:04:25,444 --> 00:04:29,374
那鞋還是他跟戴維·克羅克特掰手腕的時候
which, incidentally, were made by a 9-foot Texas diamondback

113
00:04:29,374 --> 00:04:33,094
他一腳跺死的一條近三米長的響尾蛇做成的
he stomped to death while arm-wrestling Davy Crockett.

114
00:04:33,094 --> 00:04:34,894
他的衣服都是殺動物做成的嗎
Did he kill all his clothes?

115
00:04:34,894 --> 00:04:37,094
是啊 來上樓 我給你看看
He sure did. Come upstairs. I'll show you.

116
00:04:37,094 --> 00:04:39,263
我留著一個他的戒指 里面有顆牙
I got a ring of his with a tooth in it

117
00:04:39,380 --> 00:04:40,640
是他從美洲獅嘴里打下來的
he punched out of a puma.

118
00:04:42,080 --> 00:04:43,500
杰總是這樣
Jay does this all the time.

119
00:04:43,500 --> 00:04:45,940
他不尊重我們家族 吹噓自己的
He disrespects our heritage and inflates his own.

120
00:04:45,980 --> 00:04:48,520
我一點都不相信什么先祖伊拉茲馬斯的故事
I mean, I'm not buying this Uncle Erasmus guy at all.

121
00:04:48,560 --> 00:04:49,760
我建議我們探究一下
I say we do a little digging.

122
00:04:50,060 --> 00:04:53,600
好 我們可以像托爾圖加偵探一樣
Yes! We can be like Inspector Tortuga,

123
00:04:53,960 --> 00:04:56,480
先祖阿爾瓦多大受歡迎的兒童書里的
the turtle detective in Uncle Alvaro's

124
00:04:56,480 --> 00:04:57,880
那個烏龜偵探
popular children's book.

125
00:04:58,073 --> 00:05:02,543
他總是慢慢地偵破罪案
He was always very slowly solving crimes.

126
00:05:02,903 --> 00:05:06,443
杰的先祖1830年左右確實住在德克薩斯
Turns out Jay's Uncle Erasmus did live in Texas in the 1830s,

127
00:05:06,443 --> 00:05:08,093
但是關于他的描寫不多
but not much was written about him.

128
00:05:14,323 --> 00:05:15,713
-格雷琴 -曼尼爾
- Gretchen. - Manuel.

129
00:05:15,713 --> 00:05:16,903
再一次 我非常抱歉
Again, I'm so sorry abou--

130
00:05:17,100 --> 00:05:18,620
這些書你必須兩周內還回來
You'll have to return these within two weeks.

131
00:05:18,780 --> 00:05:19,860
不像我的電話 你過了兩周都不回
Unlike my phone calls!

132
00:05:21,673 --> 00:05:23,023
臭小子
Senor.

133
00:05:23,300 --> 00:05:25,760
我們必須深入挖掘 既然歷史
We had to dig deeper, and since history

134
00:05:25,760 --> 00:05:27,340
是由勝利者書寫的
is written by the victors...

135
00:05:30,280 --> 00:05:31,000
非常感謝
Muchas gracias.

136
00:05:31,380 --> 00:05:32,660
我帶了自己的
I brought my own.

137
00:05:33,332 --> 00:05:35,282
墨西哥的資料對他在阿拉莫戰役中
Mexican sources had a bit more to say

138
00:05:35,400 --> 00:05:37,720
真實的表現描寫得更多一點
about his actual involvement in the Alamo.

139
00:05:38,212 --> 00:05:43,902
-好了 -真的嗎
- Okay. - Oh, really?

140
00:05:43,960 --> 00:05:46,220
你要把我給女兒買的第一件古馳衛衣
You want to give away the very first Gucci hoodie

141
00:05:46,220 --> 00:05:48,480
-送人嗎 -行了 就是因為買了那么多貴衣服
- I ever bought our daughter? - Okay, "First Gucci"

142
00:05:48,480 --> 00:05:50,980
退休規劃師才不給我們當顧問了
is why our retirement planner fired us as clients.

143
00:05:51,260 --> 00:05:53,280
而且 海莉和迪倫的孩子是雙胞胎
Also, Haley and Dylan are having twins, okay?

144
00:05:53,280 --> 00:05:54,600
-他們真的需要這些東西 -我知道
- They really need this stuff. - I know.

145
00:05:54,632 --> 00:05:56,832
我還是不能相信她懷孕了
I-I-I still can't believe she's pregnant.

146
00:05:57,180 --> 00:05:58,940
-不過 -我知道你要說什么賤話了
- Although... - I know you're about to say something catty.

147
00:05:59,060 --> 00:05:59,900
你都要射出賤氣了
You're practically purring.

148
00:06:00,052 --> 00:06:02,772
克萊爾二十幾歲的時候不是也"挺會玩"嗎
Wasn't Claire a bit "fun" on her 20s?

149
00:06:02,772 --> 00:06:04,412
你知道 我們老家有句俗話
You know, we have a saying back home --

150
00:06:04,420 --> 00:06:06,940
"有其母必有其女"
"The crawdad don't skitter far from its crick."

151
00:06:07,182 --> 00:06:08,802
你手里拿著名牌衣服
Okay, you're clutching a Dolce & Gabbana onesie.

152
00:06:08,802 --> 00:06:09,891
你到底想當都市人還是鄉下人
Decide who you are.

153
00:06:10,060 --> 00:06:11,700
再說了 你們家也有
And, by the way, it's not like your family

154
00:06:11,700 --> 00:06:13,660
一個惹事生非的家伙 好嗎
doesn't have a wayward streak, okay?

155
00:06:13,820 --> 00:06:15,380
小帕可沒多可靠
Pam's not exactly responsible.

156
00:06:15,520 --> 00:06:17,660
不好意思 一個不可靠的女人
Oh, I'm sorry. Could an irresponsible woman

157
00:06:17,660 --> 00:06:19,540
能在監獄獲得"最有進步摔跤手"的獎嗎
win her prison's "Most Improved Wrestler" Award?

158
00:06:19,740 --> 00:06:20,760
行了 我們就承認
Okay, let's just admit

159
